// Emission of the register-allocated IR: walks the blocks in layout order
// and emits each instruction through the machine layer (m_* below, which
// dispatches to mc_arm64.tach or mc_x86_64.tach).
//
// Locations depend on the position (see regalloc.tach): an
// instruction's operands are where the allocation puts them at its
// position, its result where it puts it two later. Every operand used in a
// register is in one; operands that may be anywhere (call arguments, phi
// operands, returned values) are moved into place by a parallel move, which
// also emits the allocation's own moves: in the gap before an instruction,
// and across each edge (at the end of a block with a single successor, or
// at the start of a block with a single predecessor). A value that goes to
// the stack is stored once, after its definition.
//
// The frame (offsets from sp, which does not move in the body):
//   [0, out)                 outgoing stack arguments
//   spill slots, 8 bytes each
//   saved callee-saved registers
//   frame slots (SLOTS)
// (spill slots stay close to sp, where every load and store can address
// them directly).
// The frame pointer (x29 / rbp) points at the saved frame pointer, above.

use crate::base::{
    BUFS, IntVec, STDERR, SYMS, alloc_array, buf_byte, buf_bytes, buf_clear, buf_int, buf_new,
    buf_slice, buf_str, buf_write_fd, die, free, memcmp, strlen,
};
